00:15:19,854 --> 00:15:28,048
you're just selling the answer to the problem you've created, in the sense of like you're building these models and now you're going to sell something to like protect me from them.

183
00:15:28,302 --> 00:15:29,188
What would you say to that?

184
00:15:29,742 --> 00:15:33,168
Well, first of all, I have a lot of empathy for that reaction.

185
00:15:33,518 --> 00:15:39,172
The way that I look at it is I rewind to 10 years ago, 11 years ago, before we started this company.

186
00:15:39,488 --> 00:15:40,516
I wasn't in AI.

187
00:15:40,814 --> 00:15:46,436
The reason I wanted to be an AI is because I feel like this can be the most empowering technology that has ever created.

188
00:15:46,702 --> 00:15:51,808
That AI can be something that helps everyone live the life that they want, build the life that they want, achieve their goals.

189
00:15:52,078 --> 00:15:56,356
And I just wanted to help steer it in a slightly more positive direction than it would be without me.

190
00:15:56,814 --> 00:15:59,748
So I started because I feel like this technology can uplift everyone.

191
00:16:00,208 --> 00:16:03,332
And when you look at where OpenAI is and what we're doing,

192
00:16:04,288 --> 00:16:13,188
we can see a little bit into the future, right? That what we are creating, it's not just us, right? That there's a whole field, there's a whole ecosystem, there are many actors.

193
00:16:13,486 --> 00:16:14,852
And that is itself a good thing.

194
00:16:15,118 --> 00:16:17,808
That we believe that there should be democratization of this technology.

