00:23:23,790 --> 00:23:25,572
We are building an integrated system.

283
00:23:26,062 --> 00:23:28,688
And safety and security are a core property of that.

284
00:23:29,230 --> 00:23:34,756
And so if you have safety and security lagging relative to the capability, yeah, you absolutely need to improve your safety and security.

285
00:23:35,150 --> 00:23:36,836
But our goal is to have a

286
00:23:37,888 --> 00:23:43,876
system that we are building at full force on safety and security as first class requirements.

287
00:23:44,526 --> 00:23:49,636
And so the way I would think about this is that we are up-leveling every aspect of the machine.

288
00:23:50,158 --> 00:23:57,604
We have spent the past year, past two years, up-leveling how we build our clusters, right? We now are able to train at massive, massive scale.

289
00:23:57,808 --> 00:23:58,596
We're able to

290
00:23:59,310 --> 00:24:04,996
get the whole pre-training machine, the RL machine, all of these pieces to work together in concert.

291
00:24:05,518 --> 00:24:06,884
We are building the best sandbox.

292
00:24:07,248 --> 00:24:09,892
We are adding chain of thought monitoring to all of this.

293
00:24:10,158 --> 00:24:15,876
To me, it's just saying what is the scope of delivery? What does success look like? What does good look like?

294
00:24:16,302 --> 00:24:22,848
And so the way I would think about it is that, yeah, if you jettison some requirements, you can move faster on other requirements, but that doesn't make any sense. That never makes any sense.

295
00:24:22,928 --> 00:24:32,996
That's not how engineering works. And so to me, it's we are pursuing the plan. Like we've really thought about this many times over the past.

296
00:24:33,294 --> 00:24:41,124
And you can see it in many of our writings from the charter to the preparedness framework and many other things in between, that as models get more capable,

297
00:24:41,518 --> 00:24:46,660
you have to make sure that you increase your safety and security requirements in concert.

298
00:24:46,830 --> 00:24:47,888
And that's exactly what we're doing.

299
00:24:48,366 --> 00:24:55,888
But I mean, practically, yes, I hear all that, but it does seem like what this will result in is the release cadence of models to lengthen.

